{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ונקבצו</b> — The sense of ונקבצו is that Sennacherib seized many of the people of Judah, and so it is written: כי תפש כל ערי יהודה הבצורות (II Kings 18:8)." "<b>ושמו להם ראש אחד</b> — This is Sennacherib." "<b>ועלו מן הארץ כי גדול יום יזרעאל</b> — That the iniquity of the house of Israel was punished, and behold all is for reproach and not for praise. Or the sense is: כי גדול יהיה יום אידם כיום יזרעאל. And one who interprets [it as] 'greater than the day of Jezreel' — there is no grammatical rule to drop the mem, for the matter would be the reverse. Furthermore: [regarding] mem — the sense of כי גדול — and there is no mention of mem there."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The text of comment 2 is difficult, possibly corrupt. The last two sentences appear fragmented: 'מ״ם טעם כי גדול' is obscure and 'ואין שם זכר מ״ם' may refer to a variant reading or a grammatical point about the absence of mem in the received text; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:49.602864840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}